Start no screen watcher for a Codex hook under MSYS or Cygwin (Git Bash on Windows). In a Codex 0.169.0 session under Git Bash the prompt stayed at "Running hook" while the watcher was alive, and ending the watcher released it (the reporter's session, PR 23; a harness that starts the hook as Codex does showed no wait, so the cause is not known). On Windows a dialog on the screen therefore does not set the pane to blocked, so a PermissionRequest never becomes the agent record's live approval and the chat view does not show or answer it. Lifecycle status, the rest of the agent record and mail work as before. Applied after 0010-origin-pane-boundary.patch.

diff --git a/ngterm-codex-status.sh b/ngterm-codex-status.sh
index 3f400dc2..380edce0 100755
--- a/ngterm-codex-status.sh
+++ b/ngterm-codex-status.sh
@@ -157,6 +157,8 @@ stop_watcher() {
 }
 
 start_watcher() {
+  # Under Git Bash a Codex was seen waiting at "Running hook" while the watcher lived; the cause is not known.
+  case "${OSTYPE:-}" in msys*|cygwin*|win32*) return 0 ;; esac
   local token token_file
   token_file=$(watch_file_path)
   token="$$-${RANDOM:-0}"
